# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a `for` row's entry is `$xs[k]`, a projection of its source, built from the values after the tick, R7), R3 (a dynamic's update event fires at n with the value after n, deduped by nobody, pick UD) and R8 (a key that leaves ends its row at the end of that tick).
test the_entry_is_a_projection

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Button(label="edit")
    2: Ui.Button(label="drop")
    3/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: a changed 0, edits 0")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: e0 changed 1, edits 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    3/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: b1 changed 0, edits 0")
  changed:
    3/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: e0 changed 2, edits 1")

tick 3
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="0: e1 changed 3, edits 2")
    3/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: b1 changed 1, edits 1")

tick 4
  in:
    2: click
  changed:
    3/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="1: b1 changed 2, edits 1")
  torn down:
